{% set local_problem %}
<p>North Alabama's climate is tough on wood. Hot, humid summers create perfect conditions for rot. When gutters overflow — common with heavy tree debris — water saturates fascia boards. That moisture, combined with humidity, leads to rot that often hides behind seemingly intact paint.</p>

<p>We find hidden fascia damage regularly during gutter estimates. The homeowner had no idea — but probe the wood with a screwdriver and it crumbles. Installing gutters on that wood would be throwing money away.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Wood repair involves removing damaged fascia, soffit, or trim and replacing with moisture-resistant materials. The process includes: assessing full damage extent; removing damaged sections; treating adjacent areas; installing new material; and prepping for gutter installation.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We see fascia damage constantly and know what to look for. We handle wood repair in-house — one crew, one job, one company standing behind everything.</p>

<p>Based just 15 miles away, we're accountable and responsive.</p>
{% endset %}
